From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] kernelsu-next: advertise UAPI v5 for older manager compatibility

The KernelSU-Next v3.4.2 dev-susfs kernel reports UAPI v6, while the
installed spoofed manager reports UAPI v5 and refuses to work. Advertise
v5 so older managers can proceed. Version-6 capabilities such as symbol
lookup and preinit remain present in the source; do not depend on these
capabilities from the older manager.

---
 uapi/supercall.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/uapi/supercall.h b/uapi/supercall.h
--- a/uapi/supercall.h
+++ b/uapi/supercall.h
@@ -6,7 +6,9 @@
 // 3: scoped su-session driver fd
 // 4: add KSU_GET_INFO_FLAG_BUNDLED
 // 5: add EVENT_SERVICES with a start/skip result
-// 6: add KSU_IOCTL_LOOKUP_SYMBOLS and KSU_GET_INFO_FLAG_PREINIT; modules.rc and preinit may live under /metadata/vold/ksu
-static const __u32 KERNEL_SU_UAPI_VERSION = 6;
+// Version 6 adds symbol lookup and preinit support. Older managers may require v5.
+// Compatibility caveat: v6 functionality is still compiled in but is not advertised.
+static const __u32 KERNEL_SU_UAPI_VERSION = 5;
 
 /* Magic numbers for reboot hook to install fd */
 static const __u32 KSU_INSTALL_MAGIC1 = 0xDEADBEEF;
